    source: "{\n \"cells\": [\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"# Hello, Diluvium\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"Diluvium is Lua 5.5 with some additions. This notebook is the shortest\\n\",\n    \"path to having run some, and a map of where the rest is.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"**Run a cell with Ctrl+Enter.** Shift+Enter runs it and moves on.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"print(\\\"hello, world\\\")\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## Cells share one kernel\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"Every cell runs in the same Lua state, in order. A global set in one\\n\",\n    \"cell is there in the next \\u2014 which is the whole point of a notebook and\\n\",\n    \"the thing that makes running cells out of order confusing.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"Run this one twice.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"counter = (counter or 0) + 1\\n\",\n    \"print(\\\"this cell has run \\\" .. counter .. \\\" time(s)\\\")\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## A cell ending in an expression shows its value\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"No `print` needed. The value appears as `Out[n]`, and tables show their\\n\",\n    \"contents rather than `table: 0x1f2e0`.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"2 ^ 10\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"{ name = \\\"ada\\\", tags = { \\\"maths\\\", \\\"engines\\\" }, year = 1843 }\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"`print` is left exactly as Lua defines it \\u2014 a notebook that quietly\\n\",\n    \"redefined it would teach you something that stops being true the moment\\n\",\n    \"you run the same code in a terminal. The `Out[n]` echo is the notebook's\\n\",\n    \"own affordance and is fair game.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## Errors keep the runtime's own words\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"With the line number, and a traceback where there is one. Under it you\\n\",\n    \"will sometimes find a plain-English hint \\u2014 the hint is *additive*, never\\n\",\n    \"a rewrite, so the message stays the one you can search for.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {\n    \"diluvium_lab\": {\n     \"expect\": \"error\"\n    }\n   },\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"local t = nil\\n\",\n    \"print(t.field)\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"Errors are catchable, which on a WebAssembly build is not a given:\\n\",\n    \"`pcall` needs `setjmp`/`longjmp` lowered onto WASM exception handling.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"print(pcall(function() error(\\\"caught\\\") end))\\n\",\n    \"print(select(2, pcall(error, { code = 42 })).code)\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## Strings interpolate\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"`$\\\"...\\\"` is Diluvium's, not stock Lua's. Everything after `::` inside a\\n\",\n    \"slot goes to `string.format`.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"local who, count = \\\"world\\\", 3\\n\",\n    \"print($\\\"hello {who}, {count} times\\\")\\n\",\n    \"print($\\\"pi to four places: {math.pi::%.4f}\\\")\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## What else is here\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"| Button | What it does |\\n\",\n    \"| :--- | :--- |\\n\",\n    \"| **Bytecode** | compiles the cell and shows the disassembly. Nothing runs. |\\n\",\n    \"| **Sandbox** | runs the cell as an isolated instance with an instruction budget |\\n\",\n    \"| **Runtime** | switches which Diluvium build the notebook runs on |\\n\",\n    \"| **\\u26f6** | puts a cell's output full screen |\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"And the console at the bottom shares this same kernel, so a variable set\\n\",\n    \"there is set here.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"**Ctrl+Space** completes names, through tables and metatables. **Tab**\\n\",\n    \"indents, **Ctrl+/** comments.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"-- put the cursor after the dot and press Ctrl+Space\\n\",\n    \"-- string.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## Where to go next\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"Open **Start here** in the toolbar for the rest:\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"- **The 5.5 language** \\u2014 `switch`, `defer`, safe navigation, compound\\n\",\n    \"  assignment, and the rest of what Diluvium adds to Lua.\\n\",\n    \"- **Secure functions** \\u2014 `~function`, what it hides and what it does not.\\n\",\n    \"- **Messages and queues** \\u2014 msgpack and the queue API.\\n\",\n    \"- **Sandboxed instances** \\u2014 budgets, and watching a program cost something.\\n\",\n    \"- **Showing things** \\u2014 plots, event streams and controls.\\n\",\n    \"- **Browser check** \\u2014 what this browser and this build actually support.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"metadata\": {\n  \"title\": \"Hello, Diluvium\",\n  \"diluvium_lab\": {\n   \"summary\": \"Start here. What a cell is, how the kernel remembers, and where everything else lives.\"\n  },\n  \"kernelspec\": {\n   \"display_name\": \"Diluvium\",\n   \"language\": \"lua\",\n   \"name\": \"diluvium\"\n  },\n  \"language_info\": {\n   \"name\": \"lua\",\n   \"file_extension\": \".lua\"\n  }\n },\n \"nbformat\": 4,\n \"nbformat_minor\": 5\n}\n",
